{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"A\n    \n      Widget-per-module — Recommended\n      Each module (audio, network, bluetooth, etc.) is a self-contained TypeScript file that exports a bar button + its dropdown panel. One shared popup manager controls which panel is open.\n      \n      \n        \n          Pros\n          \n            Each module is independent — add/remove without touching other code\n            Easy to iterate on one module without breaking others\n            Clear file structure: widgets/audio.tsx, widgets/network.tsx\n            Shared popup manager handles open/close, positioning, click-outside-to-dismiss\n          \n        \n        \n          Cons\n          \n            Some shared patterns (sliders, toggle rows) need extracting into common components\n            Popup manager adds a bit of coordination complexity\n          \n        \n      \n      \n      Structure:\n      ags/\n├── app.ts                  # Entry point, window definitions\n├── bar/\n│   ├── Bar.tsx             # Bar layout (left/center/right)\n│   └── PopupManager.ts    # Singleton: tracks open popup, handles dismiss\n├── widgets/\n│   ├── workspaces.tsx      # Workspace buttons\n│   ├── window-title.tsx    # Active window display\n│   ├── audio.tsx           # Button + dropdown panel\n│   ├── network.tsx         # Button + dropdown panel\n│   ├── bluetooth.tsx       # Button + dropdown panel\n│   ├── battery.tsx         # Button + TLP dropdown panel\n│   ├── system-stats.tsx    # Button + unified CPU/mem/temp panel\n│   ├── clock.tsx           # Button + calendar dropdown\n│   ├── media.tsx           # Now-playing bar widget + controls\n│   ├── notifications.tsx   # Bell + notification center panel\n│   └── power.tsx           # Power menu dropdown\n├── components/\n│   ├── Slider.tsx          # Reusable volume/brightness slider\n│   ├── ToggleRow.tsx       # Label + toggle switch row\n│   └── DeviceList.tsx      # Reusable device list (BT/audio)\n└── styles/\n    └── style.css           # GTK4 CSS — replaces your current waybar style","choice":"a","id":null,"timestamp":1774801805272}
